From de67e1fc81c0adca730fa1d75001b5abbee0b2eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 05:47:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Colab pip resolver conflicts: drop hard version pins in
 notebook installs

Colab ships numpy 2.x and pins dozens of pre-installed packages (jax,
cupy, opencv, shap, tifffile, google-colab itself, etc.) to numpy>=2.
The previous notebooks pinned numpy==1.26.4 (and matching pandas/
scikit-learn/joblib/requests versions) in every !pip install cell,
which forced pip to downgrade numpy and broke every one of those
pre-installed packages, hanging or erroring out the very first cell.

Fix: install cells now request packages by name only (prophet,
xgboost, scikit-learn, pandas, numpy, networkx, joblib, requests,
simpy) with no version pins, so pip leaves Colab's already-satisfied
pre-installed packages alone and only fetches what's actually missing
(prophet, xgboost, simpy). requirements.txt for the FastAPI backend is
unaffected - that runs in an isolated venv where pinning is safe and
desirable.
